ore), and in any event the rider did state a sub-location. Your account that the app pin showed the carpark side is not corroborated: no fix in your track carries a venue_id, so under POL-NS-03 the venue point is simply not established either way and the distance test governs alone. That same rule bars the rider's suggestion that you waited at 'block 128'; it is the same-or-different-block assertion POL-NS-03 forbids on general knowledge, and nothing is built on it here. Because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full, POL-NS-07 pays no compensation, and POL-NS-03(i) puts the loss on you; driver compensation is therefore nil.\n\nEvidence weight: the chat log EV-CHAT-00205 is impaired at weight 0.8 (issue CONTENT_REDACTED). The redaction removed only the unit number; the block identifier that the fault finding turns on survives intact, so the finding survives the discount. The artifacts carrying the deciding fact — that the driver never arrived at the pickup point — are the GPS trace and the trip record, both at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) confidence cap is 1.0. The chat's impairment is schema-level only: it does not meet POL-NS-08(a)–(d) (4 messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count 4, contiguous msg_ids, no gap over 5 minutes across the arrival marker), so it is down-weighted under POL-GEN-02 and does not engage the impairment sentence of POL-NS-08.\n\nNo escalation: the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below 4, and 2/104 = 0.019, below 0.08); rider no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below 3; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; and the deciding fact is carried by full-weight evidence, not by an artifact impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d), so the POL-NS-09(a)–(e) triggers are not met. No context-only profile field (rating, account age, lifetime trips, cancellation rate, prior flags) was used as a ground of decision.\n\nNo false-arrival 